{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Ve38QsZn8UkPCqxYsxn2F","type":"tool_result","content":"1\texperiments:\n2\t  # === P0: Core submission (must complete for EACL 2027 ARR Aug 3) ===\n3\t\n4\t  - id: plan_001\n5\t    claim: 1\n6\t    description: >\n7\t      Full Pareto frontier on Qwen3-235B-A22B (94 layers, MoE, INT8):\n8\t      extract activations at every 4th layer (24 probed layers),\n9\t      20 typologically diverse languages, train English correctness probes\n10\t      (logistic regression + 2-layer MLP), evaluate 5 transfer conditions\n11\t      (zero-shot, mean-shift, linear projection, few-shot 25/100, CaCLR).\n12\t      Report per-language Spearman rho (depth vs transfer AUROC) alongside global rho.\n13\t    priority: P0\n14\t    gpu_budget_hours: 80\n15\t    deps: []\n16\t    notes: \"Needs 3-4× RTX 6000 PRO 96GB at INT8. May need GPU upgrade request.\"\n17\t\n18\t  - id: plan_002\n19\t    claim: 1\n20\t    description: >\n21\t      Full Pareto frontier on Llama 4 Scout (48 layers, MoE, INT8):\n22\t      extract activations at every 4th layer (12 probed layers),\n23\t      20 languages, 5 transfer conditions. INT8 weight quantization.\n24\t      Report per-language Spearman rho (depth vs transfer AUROC) alongside global rho.\n25\t    priority: P0\n26\t    gpu_budget_hours: 40\n27\t    deps: []\n28\t    notes: \"Needs 2× RTX 6000 PRO 96GB at INT8.\"\n29\t\n30\t  - id: plan_003\n31\t    claim: 3\n32\t    description: >\n33\t      CaCLR implementation and comparative evaluation:\n34\t      L_CaCLR = L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_consistency (MMD distance).\n35\t      Train CaCLR probes using English labels + unlabeled parallel activations\n36\t      (GlobalMMLU train split translations, not test items).\n37\t      Compare vs zero-shot, mean-shift, linear projection, few-shot (25/100)\n38\t      across full Pareto frontier for both models × 20 languages.\n39\t      Hyperparameter tuning: α sweep (0.01-10.0), β sweep across 3 OOM (0.001-1.0).\n40\t      Report fixed-layer results (50% depth + EN-optimal) alongside per-language oracle.\n41\t    priority: P0\n42\t    gpu_budget_hours: 20\n43\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n44\t    notes: >\n45\t      CPU-bound once activations cached. SB-ECE from Karandikar et al. NeurIPS 2021.\n46\t      L_consistency uses Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD).\n47\t      If β sweep shows inert consistency loss, reframe as negative result (see paper_framing.md Claim 3 conditional narrative).\n48\t\n49\t  - id: plan_004\n50\t    claim: 2\n51\t    description: >\n52\t      Difficulty-controlled ablation: train IRT difficulty probes (Ridge regression\n53\t      on human difficulty scores per Civelli et al.), project out difficulty direction\n54\t      from activations, retrain correctness probes on residuals, evaluate transfer.\n55\t      10 representative languages × 8 representative layers per model (20-90% depth).\n56\t    priority: P0\n57\t    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n58\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n59\t    notes: >\n60\t      Need IRT difficulty scores from GlobalMMLU or external source.\n61\t      Grid justification (D12): 10 languages cover 3 resource tiers (HIGH: zh/es/fr/de, MID: hi/ru/ko/tr, LOW: sw/bn)\n62\t      × major language families. 8 layers span 20-90% depth at uniform intervals.\n63\t      Reduced grid is sufficient because decomposition tests a qualitative hypothesis\n64\t      (does projecting out difficulty help or hurt?), not a per-language quantitative claim.\n65\t      Include random-direction control to rule out dimensionality-reduction artifacts.\n66\t\n67\t  # === Cross-cutting requirement (Dream review D1) ===\n68\t  # All experiments must include: bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples),\n69\t  # paired permutation tests for key comparisons, Cohen's d for effect sizes.\n70\t  # Report GlobalMMLU sample sizes per language.\n71\t  # AUROC threshold sensitivity analysis (0.55/0.60/0.65/0.70/0.75) for pass/fail reporting.\n72\t\n73\t  # === P1: Important for strong submission ===\n74\t\n75\t  - id: plan_005\n76\t    claim: 4\n77\t    description: >\n78\t      Cross-lingual orthogonality analysis: extract verbalized confidence direction\n79\t      (prompt model for confidence score, fit probe), compute cosine similarity\n80\t      with correctness direction across 20 languages × 2 architectures.\n81\t      Analyze by resource tier (high/mid/low) and language family.\n82\t    priority: P1\n83\t    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n84\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n85\t\n86\t  - id: plan_006\n87\t    claim: 1\n88\t    description: >\n89\t      Probe complexity comparison: logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP\n90\t      at each probed layer for both models. Compare English accuracy,\n91\t      cross-lingual transfer degradation, and calibration quality.\n92\t      Test hypothesis: linear probes transfer better cross-lingually.\n93\t    priority: P1\n94\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n95\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n96\t    notes: \"CPU-bound, uses cached activations.\"\n97\t\n98\t  - id: plan_007\n99\t    claim: 1\n100\t    description: >\n101\t      Additional benchmark evaluation: evaluate best probes + CaCLR\n102\t      on Belebele (20 languages) and MMLU-ProX (20 languages).\n103\t      Validates generalization beyond MMLU/GlobalMMLU.\n104\t    priority: P1\n105\t    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n106\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002, plan_003]\n107\t\n108\t  - id: plan_010\n109\t    claim: 1\n110\t    description: >\n111\t      INT8 validation ablation: compare INT8 vs FP16 probing results\n112\t      at 5 representative layers for Llama 4 Scout on 5% random subset.\n113\t      Validates that INT8 quantization doesn't distort correctness signals.\n114\t    priority: P1\n115\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n116\t    deps: [plan_002]\n117\t\n118\t  - id: plan_011\n119\t    claim: [1, 4]\n120\t    description: >\n121\t      CKA cross-lingual representation similarity analysis:\n122\t      compute CKA (linear kernel) between English and each target language\n123\t      at every probed layer for both models. Full-scale validation of pilot finding:\n124\t      correctness direction is a robust low-dimensional subspace feature that persists\n125\t      despite global CKA decline. Transfer collapses only at critical CKA threshold (~0.35).\n126\t      Report CKA × layer × language heatmaps, CKA vs transfer degradation\n127\t      ((EN_AUROC - target_AUROC) / EN_AUROC) correlation per language to isolate\n128\t      alignment effect from probe quality, and critical threshold analysis.\n129\t    priority: P1\n130\t    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n131\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n132\t    notes: >\n133\t      CKA pilot COMPLETED on mvp_001/mvp_003 (5 langs × 8-9 layers × 2 models).\n134\t      Key finding: CKA vs AUROC negatively correlated (rho=-0.16 overall, hi rho=-0.79 sig,\n135\t      sw rho=-0.88 sig). Correctness signal is robust to global representation divergence.\n136\t      Original hypothesis (\"low CKA → bad transfer\") REVISED to threshold model.\n137\t      Full-scale run validates at 20 languages × 24/12 layers × 2 large models.\n138\t\n139\t  - id: plan_012\n140\t    claim: 1\n141\t    description: >\n142\t      Linear projection sensitivity analysis: vary number of parallel\n143\t      pairs (10, 20, 50, 100, 200) for linear projection transfer.\n144\t      Determines minimum data requirement for this surprisingly strong baseline.\n145\t      Both models × 5 representative layers × 20 languages.\n146\t    priority: P1\n147\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n148\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n149\t    notes: \"CPU-bound, uses cached activations. Dream review D11.\"\n150\t\n151\t  - id: plan_013\n152\t    claim: 1\n153\t    description: >\n154\t      Probing control tasks (Hewitt & Liang 2019): train probes on\n155\t      randomly permuted labels at each layer. Compare selectivity\n156\t      (probe AUROC - control AUROC) across layers and languages.\n157\t      Validates that high AUROC reflects genuine correctness direction,\n158\t      not memorized dataset artifacts or probe capacity.\n159\t    priority: P1\n160\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n161\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n162\t    notes: \"CPU-bound. Dream review D22: probing methodology critique.\"\n163\t\n164\t  # === P2: Camera-ready extension ===\n165\t\n166\t  - id: plan_008\n167\t    claim: 1\n168\t    description: >\n169\t      Gemma 4 31B Dense (60 layers, dense, FP16): third architecture\n170\t      for camera-ready. Full Pareto frontier, 20+ languages.\n171\t      Provides dense vs MoE architectural contrast.\n172\t    priority: P2\n173\t    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n174\t    deps: []\n175\t\n176\t  - id: plan_009\n177\t    claim: 1\n178\t    description: >\n179\t      Extended language coverage: expand from 20 to 50+ languages\n180\t      for camera-ready. Leverages GlobalMMLU/Belebele full language sets.\n181\t    priority: P2\n182\t    gpu_budget_hours: 50\n183\t    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n184\t\n185\t  # === MVP experiments (completed/running) ===\n186\t\n187\t  - id: mvp_validation\n188\t    claim: 1\n189\t    description: \"MVP: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, 6 languages, 8 layers, zero-shot + mean-shift\"\n190\t    priority: P0\n191\t    registry_id: mvp_001\n192\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n193\t    deps: []\n194\t\n195\t  - id: mvp_complementary\n196\t    claim: 1\n197\t    description: \"MVP robustness: complementary layer set (2,6,10,14,18,22,26)\"\n198\t    priority: P1\n199\t    registry_id: mvp_002\n200\t    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n201\t    deps: [mvp_validation]\n202\t\n203\t  - id: mvp_llama_control\n204\t    claim: 1\n205\t    description: \"MVP cross-architecture: Llama-3.1-8B control experiment\"\n206\t    priority: P1\n207\t    registry_id: mvp_003\n208\t    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n209\t    deps: [mvp_validation]\n210\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3372ce2-16de-4b98-b026-560c840f0560","uuid":"7c537a5a-2e6a-46d5-9f82-8cd4106ca711","timestamp":"2026-05-20T20:31:53.722Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0519_2/projects/xling_calib_direction/experiment_plan.yaml","content":"experiments:\n  # === P0: Core submission (must complete for EACL 2027 ARR Aug 3) ===\n\n  - id: plan_001\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Full Pareto frontier on Qwen3-235B-A22B (94 layers, MoE, INT8):\n      extract activations at every 4th layer (24 probed layers),\n      20 typologically diverse languages, train English correctness probes\n      (logistic regression + 2-layer MLP), evaluate 5 transfer conditions\n      (zero-shot, mean-shift, linear projection, few-shot 25/100, CaCLR).\n      Report per-language Spearman rho (depth vs transfer AUROC) alongside global rho.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 80\n    deps: []\n    notes: \"Needs 3-4× RTX 6000 PRO 96GB at INT8. May need GPU upgrade request.\"\n\n  - id: plan_002\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Full Pareto frontier on Llama 4 Scout (48 layers, MoE, INT8):\n      extract activations at every 4th layer (12 probed layers),\n      20 languages, 5 transfer conditions. INT8 weight quantization.\n      Report per-language Spearman rho (depth vs transfer AUROC) alongside global rho.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 40\n    deps: []\n    notes: \"Needs 2× RTX 6000 PRO 96GB at INT8.\"\n\n  - id: plan_003\n    claim: 3\n    description: >\n      CaCLR implementation and comparative evaluation:\n      L_CaCLR = L_BCE + α·L_SB-ECE + β·L_consistency (MMD distance).\n      Train CaCLR probes using English labels + unlabeled parallel activations\n      (GlobalMMLU train split translations, not test items).\n      Compare vs zero-shot, mean-shift, linear projection, few-shot (25/100)\n      across full Pareto frontier for both models × 20 languages.\n      Hyperparameter tuning: α sweep (0.01-10.0), β sweep across 3 OOM (0.001-1.0).\n      Report fixed-layer results (50% depth + EN-optimal) alongside per-language oracle.\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 20\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n    notes: >\n      CPU-bound once activations cached. SB-ECE from Karandikar et al. NeurIPS 2021.\n      L_consistency uses Maximum Mean Discrepancy (MMD).\n      If β sweep shows inert consistency loss, reframe as negative result (see paper_framing.md Claim 3 conditional narrative).\n\n  - id: plan_004\n    claim: 2\n    description: >\n      Difficulty-controlled ablation: train IRT difficulty probes (Ridge regression\n      on human difficulty scores per Civelli et al.), project out difficulty direction\n      from activations, retrain correctness probes on residuals, evaluate transfer.\n      10 representative languages × 8 representative layers per model (20-90% depth).\n    priority: P0\n    gpu_budget_hours: 15\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n    notes: >\n      Need IRT difficulty scores from GlobalMMLU or external source.\n      Grid justification (D12): 10 languages cover 3 resource tiers (HIGH: zh/es/fr/de, MID: hi/ru/ko/tr, LOW: sw/bn)\n      × major language families. 8 layers span 20-90% depth at uniform intervals.\n      Reduced grid is sufficient because decomposition tests a qualitative hypothesis\n      (does projecting out difficulty help or hurt?), not a per-language quantitative claim.\n      Include random-direction control to rule out dimensionality-reduction artifacts.\n\n  # === Cross-cutting requirement (Dream review D1) ===\n  # All experiments must include: bootstrap CIs (1000 resamples),\n  # paired permutation tests for key comparisons, Cohen's d for effect sizes.\n  # Report GlobalMMLU sample sizes per language.\n  # AUROC threshold sensitivity analysis (0.55/0.60/0.65/0.70/0.75) for pass/fail reporting.\n\n  # === P1: Important for strong submission ===\n\n  - id: plan_005\n    claim: 4\n    description: >\n      Cross-lingual orthogonality analysis: extract verbalized confidence direction\n      (prompt model for confidence score, fit probe), compute cosine similarity\n      with correctness direction across 20 languages × 2 architectures.\n      Analyze by resource tier (high/mid/low) and language family.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 10\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n\n  - id: plan_006\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Probe complexity comparison: logistic regression vs 2-layer MLP\n      at each probed layer for both models. Compare English accuracy,\n      cross-lingual transfer degradation, and calibration quality.\n      Test hypothesis: linear probes transfer better cross-lingually.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n    notes: \"CPU-bound, uses cached activations.\"\n\n  - id: plan_007\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Additional benchmark evaluation: evaluate best probes + CaCLR\n      on Belebele (20 languages) and MMLU-ProX (20 languages).\n      Validates generalization beyond MMLU/GlobalMMLU.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002, plan_003]\n\n  - id: plan_010\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      INT8 validation ablation: compare INT8 vs FP16 probing results\n      at 5 representative layers for Llama 4 Scout on 5% random subset.\n      Validates that INT8 quantization doesn't distort correctness signals.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n    deps: [plan_002]\n\n  - id: plan_011\n    claim: [1, 4]\n    description: >\n      CKA cross-lingual representation similarity analysis:\n      compute CKA (linear kernel) between English and each target language\n      at every probed layer for both models. Full-scale validation of pilot finding:\n      correctness direction is a robust low-dimensional subspace feature that persists\n      despite global CKA decline. Transfer collapses only at critical CKA threshold (~0.35).\n      Report CKA × layer × language heatmaps, CKA vs transfer degradation\n      ((EN_AUROC - target_AUROC) / EN_AUROC) correlation per language to isolate\n      alignment effect from probe quality, and critical threshold analysis.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 5\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n    notes: >\n      CKA pilot COMPLETED on mvp_001/mvp_003 (5 langs × 8-9 layers × 2 models).\n      Key finding: CKA vs AUROC negatively correlated (rho=-0.16 overall, hi rho=-0.79 sig,\n      sw rho=-0.88 sig). Correctness signal is robust to global representation divergence.\n      Original hypothesis (\"low CKA → bad transfer\") REVISED to threshold model.\n      Full-scale run validates at 20 languages × 24/12 layers × 2 large models.\n\n  - id: plan_012\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Linear projection sensitivity analysis: vary number of parallel\n      pairs (10, 20, 50, 100, 200) for linear projection transfer.\n      Determines minimum data requirement for this surprisingly strong baseline.\n      Both models × 5 representative layers × 20 languages.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n    notes: \"CPU-bound, uses cached activations. Dream review D11.\"\n\n  - id: plan_013\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Probing control tasks (Hewitt & Liang 2019): train probes on\n      randomly permuted labels at each layer. Compare selectivity\n      (probe AUROC - control AUROC) across layers and languages.\n      Validates that high AUROC reflects genuine correctness direction,\n      not memorized dataset artifacts or probe capacity.\n    priority: P1\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n    notes: \"CPU-bound. Dream review D22: probing methodology critique.\"\n\n  # === P2: Camera-ready extension ===\n\n  - id: plan_008\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Gemma 4 31B Dense (60 layers, dense, FP16): third architecture\n      for camera-ready. Full Pareto frontier, 20+ languages.\n      Provides dense vs MoE architectural contrast.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 30\n    deps: []\n\n  - id: plan_009\n    claim: 1\n    description: >\n      Extended language coverage: expand from 20 to 50+ languages\n      for camera-ready. Leverages GlobalMMLU/Belebele full language sets.\n    priority: P2\n    gpu_budget_hours: 50\n    deps: [plan_001, plan_002]\n\n  # === MVP experiments (completed/running) ===\n\n  - id: mvp_validation\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"MVP: Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct, 6 languages, 8 layers, zero-shot + mean-shift\"\n    priority: P0\n    registry_id: mvp_001\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: []\n\n  - id: mvp_complementary\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"MVP robustness: complementary layer set (2,6,10,14,18,22,26)\"\n    priority: P1\n    registry_id: mvp_002\n    gpu_budget_hours: 2\n    deps: [mvp_validation]\n\n  - id: mvp_llama_control\n    claim: 1\n    description: \"MVP cross-architecture: Llama-3.1-8B control experiment\"\n    priority: P1\n    registry_id: mvp_003\n    gpu_budget_hours: 3\n    deps: [mvp_validation]\n","numLines":210,"startLine":1,"totalLines":210}}}
